00:34:44,499 --> 00:34:50,283
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, it's not necessarily going to be going to be, you know, a nice ride right away.

342
00:34:51,043 --> 00:35:00,449
[SPEAKER_00]: Obviously, eventually, you want to be free from suffering, but you have to recognize, like anything, in the beginning, it's always a grind, so to say.

343
00:35:00,749 --> 00:35:00,969
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

344
00:35:02,450 --> 00:35:03,610
[SPEAKER_03]: And I think that's very important.

345
00:35:03,630 --> 00:35:07,513
[SPEAKER_03]: Like what you said also, Lapandu, recognizing one's own attitude.

346
00:35:08,251 --> 00:35:23,581
[SPEAKER_03]: Like, link to what you just said, because if one doesn't recognize that, okay, I'm actually wanting to get rid of that, so I'm acting out of aversion and craving, like, my whole practice is based on that, so everything that I can recognize as peaceful or as pleasant is actually

347
00:35:29,595 --> 00:35:33,857
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, and doesn't matter how peaceful it is, it is within the same container.

348
00:35:33,897 --> 00:35:58,230
[SPEAKER_00]: So then, that's why, if it is... if it just comes easily to you, kind of at the same time or parallel to your lay life and your possessions and your worldly engagements, and you kind of have it side by side like that, that's a good indication that this other thing is just coming basically within the same... taking place within those same attitudes.

349
00:35:58,950 --> 00:35:59,892
[SPEAKER_00]: that you are used to.

350
00:36:00,092 --> 00:36:06,463
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it didn't require you to transform your your mind, your way of existing.

351
00:36:07,164 --> 00:36:09,849
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, just imagine if you had a dog that was

352
00:36:11,015 --> 00:36:24,524
[SPEAKER_00]: That was wild and, you know, or a child that was that was spoiled and, you know, behaving... having bad behavior and suddenly, the next day, it's like an angel.

353
00:36:25,164 --> 00:36:33,769
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, you might be suspicious that there are some, you know, underlying... it's not a... it didn't magically change like that.

354
00:36:33,849 --> 00:36:34,130
[SPEAKER_00]: So,

355
00:36:35,030 --> 00:36:36,052
[SPEAKER_00]: The same thing with the mind.

356
00:36:36,152 --> 00:36:47,791
[SPEAKER_00]: If you have been, you know, acting out of greed, aversion, and delusion, and suddenly you find this pleasure, and it's really wonderful, and, you know, all the all the suffering is gone, well, you should be skeptical about that, because...

357
00:36:49,168 --> 00:36:53,411
[SPEAKER_03]: So, one should actually tell yourself, like, it's quite hard, but, like, I don't know what happiness is.

358
00:36:53,451 --> 00:36:57,374
[SPEAKER_03]: Like, I don't know, like, I'm suffering and I don't know how to get out.

359
00:36:57,634 --> 00:36:57,855
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

360
00:36:58,155 --> 00:36:58,715
[SPEAKER_03]: It's quite hard.

361
00:36:59,096 --> 00:37:11,305
[SPEAKER_00]: The Buddha said the whole world sees the pleasant sights, sounds, smells, tastes, touches and thoughts, like phenomena, as pleasant.

362
00:37:11,985 --> 00:37:15,188
[SPEAKER_00]: And the cessation, the actual thing that's pleasant,

363
00:37:16,327 --> 00:37:20,808
[SPEAKER_00]: ...is seen as unpleasant by the world, which is the cessation of those things.

364
00:37:21,708 --> 00:37:26,889
[SPEAKER_00]: And he says, the noble ones are the ones who understand that as the true pleasure.

365
00:37:27,429 --> 00:37:40,832
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you have to understand, like, whatever I regard as pleasure, not like I have to get rid of it, because then we get into the same thing we were discussing before, like you want to deny the significance of everything, but you can't take it as the way to enlightenment.

366
00:37:40,912 --> 00:37:42,673
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't assume that if it's pleasant,

367
00:37:44,994 --> 00:37:50,859
[SPEAKER_00]: pleasure is going to rise on its own, but it can't be taken as a vehicle.

368
00:37:51,740 --> 00:38:01,027
[SPEAKER_00]: That's when... because you end up with all sorts of misconceptions, like, you know,

369
00:38:03,420 --> 00:38:19,594
[SPEAKER_00]: Metta, for example, metta practice, like, you assume that you just generate this pleasant feeling, these pleasant feelings, and that's it, like, you're you're already practicing, you know, the... You're on the way to nibbāna, radiating these pleasant feelings all over the place, yeah.

370
00:38:19,714 --> 00:38:30,023
[SPEAKER_00]: And you never had to go through any sort of training, like, you just... everything just fit together magically like that, so that's just too good to be true, basically.

